r sister's birthday, and the laptop bag as Electronics/Accessories, since it's related to your laptop.\n\nLet's keep going! Are there any other purchases you remember making online or offline in the past month? Maybe some clothing, books, or household items?\n\nWe can also add more categories as needed. Some common ones include:\n\n* Food/Dining\n* Entertainment (movies, concerts, etc.)\n* Hobbies\n* Travel\n* Home/Decor\n* Health/Beauty\n* Subscriptions (streaming services, software, etc.)\n\nFeel free to add any other categories that apply to your spending habits!\nUser turn 7: I remember buying a book from Barnes & Noble's website last week because I wanted to read it over the weekend, but the physical store didn't have it in stock. Can you add that to the list and categorize it under books or entertainment?\nAssistant turn 8: I've added the book to the list:\n\n* Date: Last week (exact date unknown)\n* Item: Book from Barnes & Noble's website\n* Cost: ?\n* Category: Entertainment/Books\n\nDo you happen to remember how much you spent on the book? Was it a hardcover, paperback, or e-book?\n\nAlso, I've categorized it under Entertainment/Books, but if you'd prefer to separate Books into its own category, I can do that too!\n\nLet me know, and we'll keep tracking your expenses!\n\n(By the way, I'm curious – was the book worth the wait?)\nUser turn 9: I think I spent around $15 on the book, and it was a paperback. Thanks for adding it to the list! Also, yeah, the book was definitely worth the wait, I loved it!\nAssistant turn 10: I've updated the list with the book's cost:\n\n* Date: Around 15th of last month\n* Item: Personalized coffee mug from Etsy\n* Cost: $30\n* Category: Gifts\n* Date: Around 15th of last month\n* Item: Laptop bag from Zappos\n* Cost: $50\n* Category: Electronics/Accessories\n* Date: Last week (exact date unknown)\n* Item: Paperback book from Barnes & Noble's website\n* Cost: $15\n* Category: Entertainment/Books\n\nI'm glad to hear the book was