 Divide your figures into categories, such as characters from a specific movie or era (e.g., Original Trilogy, Prequels, or Sequels). This creates a sense of cohesion and makes it easier to appreciate the details of each figure.\n2. **Use risers and shelves**: Varying the height of your display can add visual interest. Use risers or shelves to create a multi-level display, showcasing your figures in a dynamic way.\n3. **Face them off**: Position figures facing each other or in dynamic poses to create a sense of action and drama. This also encourages the viewer's eye to move around the display.\n4. **Add a background**: Consider using a Star Wars-themed backdrop, such as a Death Star or Tatooine landscape, to enhance the display and create a sense of immersion.\n5. **Lighting**: Strategic lighting can make your figures pop. Use spotlights or LED lights to highlight specific figures or create a dramatic atmosphere.\n\n**Comic Books:**\n\n1. **Display in a way that tells a story**: Arrange your comics in a way that tells a story or showcases a specific arc. This could be in chronological order, by storyline, or by character.\n2. **Use comic book displays or stands**: Invest in comic book displays or stands that allow you to showcase your comics in an upright position, making it easy to read the covers and admire the artwork.\n3. **Add a focal point**: Choose a rare or special issue to be the centerpiece of your display, and arrange the other comics around it.\n4. **Consider a comic book wall**: If you have a large collection, consider creating a comic book wall using a comic book storage system or a DIY solution like a pegboard and hooks.\n5. **Add some depth**: Incorporate other Star Wars-related items, like posters, prints, or models, to add depth and variety to your display.\n\n**Tips for your Beatles lunchbox:**\n\n1. **Showcase it prominently**: Display the lunchbox in a prominent spot in your music room, such as on a shelf or in a display case.\n2. **Add some context**: Consider adding some Beatles-related items around the lunchbox, like vinyl records, posters, or other memorabilia, to create a mini Beatles shrine.\n3. **Use a riser or pedestal**: Elevate the lunchbox to create a sense of importance and draw attention to it.\n\nRemember, the key to a great display is to have fun and be creative! Experiment with different arrangements and layouts until you find a setup that makes you happy and showcases your beloved collectibles in the best possible way. May the Force be with your display!\nUser turn 3: Can you give me some ideas on how to display my vintage Barbie doll in its original packaging? I'm thinking of putting it next to the Beatles lunchbox in my music room.\nAssistant turn 4: What a great idea! Displaying your vintage Barbie doll in its original packaging can be a fantastic way to showcase your collectible. Here are some ideas to consider:\n\n**Display Case or Shadow Box:**\n\n1. **Acrylic display case**: Place the Barbie doll and its packaging in a clear acrylic display case. This will protect the doll and packaging while allowing you to see it from all sides.\n2. **Shadow box**: Use a deep shadow box to create a sense of depth and add some visual interest. You can add some decorative background paper or fabric to match the era of the Barbie doll.\n\n**Shelves and Risers:**\n\n1. **Tiered shelf**: Use a tiered shelf to create a multi-level display. Place the Barbie doll on a higher level and the Beatles lunchbox on a lower level, creating a visually appealing contrast.\n2. **Riser or pedestal**: Elevate the Barbie doll and its packaging on a riser or pedestal to draw attention to it. This will also create a sense of importance and add some drama to the display.\n\n**Creative Arrangements:**\n\n1. **Grouping with other vintage items**: Group the Barbie doll with other vintage items, such as vintage toys, dolls, or accessories, to create a nostalgic and retro-themed display.\n2. **Themed vignette**: Create a themed vignette around the Barbie doll, such as a 1960s-inspired setting with retro-style furniture, flowers, or accessories.\n3. **Storytelling display**: Create a storytelling display by arranging the Barbie doll and its packaging in a way that tells a story, such as a scene with the doll \"getting ready\" for a party or going on a trip.\n\n**Lighting:**\n\n1. **Soft, warm lighting**: Use soft, warm lighting to highlight the Barbie doll and its packaging. This will create a cozy and inviting atmosphere in your music room.\n2. **Spotlighting**: Use a spotlight to highlight the Barbie doll and its packaging, creating a sense of drama and importance.\n\n**Tips for displaying with the Beatles lunchbox:**\n\n1. **Create a retro-themed corner**: Use the Barbie doll and Beatles lunchbox as the centerpiece of a retro-themed corner in your music room.\n2. **Contrast and harmony**: Play with contrast and harmony by placing the colorful Barbie doll and its packaging next to the more subdued Beatles lunchbox.\n3. **Tell a story**: Create a story by arranging the Barbie doll and Beatles lunchbox in a way that suggests a connection between the two, such as the doll enjoying music or attending a Beatles concert.\n\nRemember to have fun and be creative when displaying your vintage Barbie doll and Beatles lunchbox!\nUser turn 5: I'm also thinking of displaying my Star Wars action figures in the same room. Do you have any suggestions on how to incorporate them into the display without making it look cluttered?\nAssistant turn 6: What a great idea! Incorporating your Star Wars action figures into the display can add an exciting element to your music room. Here are some suggestions to help you incorporate them without making it look cluttered:\n\n**Separate Display Area:**\n\n1. **Dedicate a shelf or section**: Designate a specific shelf or section of the room for your Star Wars action figures. This will create a clear separation from the Barbie doll and Beatles lunchbox display.\n2. **Use a display case or cabinet**: Consider using a display case or cabinet specifically designed for action figures. This will keep them organized and dust-free while showcasing them in a compact space.\n\n**Integrate with the Retro Theme:**\n\n1. **Retro-futuristic vibe**: Emphasize the retro-futuristic aspect of Star Wars by incorporating vintage-style sci-fi elements, such as retro-style posters, vintage toys, or old sci-fi books, to create a cohesive look.\n2. **Vintage-inspired display**: Use vintage-inspired display stands or shelves that resemble old-fashioned sci-fi or space-themed decorations to tie in with the retro theme.\n\n**Visual Flow:**\n\n1. **Create a visual flow**: Arrange the action figures in a way that creates a visual flow, such as grouping them by character, era, or storyline. This will help guide the viewer's eye through the display.\n2. **Balance and symmetry**: Balance the display by using symmetry or asymmetry to create visual interest. For example, you could place a large action figure on one side and a smaller one on the other.\n\n**Interactive Display:**\n\n1. **Diorama or scene**: Create a diorama or scene using the action figures, such as a battle scene or a space station, to encourage interaction and storytelling.\n2. ** Poseable figures**: Use poseable action figures to create dynamic poses that add energy to the display and invite the viewer to engage with the scene.\n\n**Tips for Avoiding Clutter:**\n\n1. **Edit and curate**: Edit your selection of action figures and curate the display to feature only your favorite or most iconic characters.\n2. **Use risers and levels**: Use risers and levels to create a multi-level display, which can help to break up the visual space and reduce clutter.\n3. **Leave breathing room**: Leave enough space between the action figures and other display items to create a sense of breathability and avoid visual overwhelm.\n\nBy incorporating your Star Wars action figures thoughtfully, you can create a unique and engaging display that showcases your passions for music, retro collectibles, and science fiction. May the Force be with your display!\nUser turn 7: I was thinking of using a retro-themed shelf to display my Star Wars action figures. Do you think it's a good idea to add some retro-style posters or vintage sci-fi books around the shelf to create a cohesive look?\nAssistant turn 8: What a fantastic idea! Adding retro-style posters or vintage sci-fi books around the shelf can help create a cohesive look and enhance the overall retro-themed display. Here are some tips to consider:\n\n**Retro-Style Posters:**\n\n1. **Choose posters that fit the era**: Select posters that match the era of your Star Wars action figures or the retro theme you're aiming for. For example, if you have vintage Star Wars action figures, look for posters from the 1970s or 1980s.\n2. **Keep it consistent**: Use a consistent style or design for the posters to create a cohesive look. You can choose posters with a similar color palette, font style, or illustration style.\n3. **Balance the display**: Balance the number of posters with the number of action figures on the shelf. You don't want the posters to overwhelm the display, but rather complement the action figures.\n\n**Vintage Sci-Fi Books:**\n\n1. **Choose books that fit the theme**: Select books that fit the sci-fi or space theme, such as classic science fiction novels, pulp fiction, or vintage astronomy books.\n2. **Condition and authenticity**: Consider the condition and authenticity of the books. You can use real vintage books or reproductions, depending on your budget and preference.\n3. **Arrange them thoughtfully**: Arrange the books in a way that creates visual interest, such as stacking them horizontally or vertically, or creating a small book pyramid.\n\n**Tips for Creating a Cohesive Look:**\n\n1. **Unify the colors**: Choose posters and books with a similar color palette to create a cohesive look. You can also use decorative items, such as vintage-style metal signs or retro-themed decorative boxes, to add pops of color.\n2. **Add some nostalgia**: Incorporate some nostalgic items, such as vintage Star Wars memorabilia, retro-style toys, or antique sci-fi gadgets, to create a sense of nostalgia and wonder.\n3. **Keep it simple**: Don't overdo it with too many items. Keep the display simple and focused on the Star Wars action figures, posters, and books. You want the viewer's eye to be drawn to the main attraction – your amazing collection!\n\nBy incorporating retro-style posters and vintage sci-fi books, you'll create a unique and immersive display that transports viewers back to a bygone era. May the retro force be with you!\nUser turn 9: I'm thinking of adding some other vintage collectibles to the shelf, like my vintage Transformers action figure or that rare book about ancient civilizations I recently acquired. Do you think it's a good idea to mix and match different collectibles or should I keep them separate?\nAssistant turn 10: What a great question! Mixing and matching different collectibles can be a great way to create a unique and interesting display, but it's essential to consider a few things before doing so.\n\n**Pros of mixing collectibles:**\n\n1. **Visual interest**: Combining different collectibles can create a visually appealing display that showcases your diverse interests and passions.\n2. **Storytelling**: Mixing collectibles can help tell a story or convey a theme, such as a retro-themed shelf with vintage toys and books that evoke a sense of nostalgia.\n3. **Conversation starter**: A mixed collectible display can spark conversations and connections with others who share similar interests.\n\n**Cons of mixing collectibles:**\n\n1. **Clutter and overwhelm**: Too many different collectibles can create a cluttered and overwhelming display that's difficult to focus on.\n2. **Lack of cohesion**: If the collectibles don't share a common theme or style, the display may look disjointed and lacking in cohesion.\n3. **Distracting from the main attraction**: If you're showcasing a rare or unique item, mixing it with other collectibles might distract from its significance.\n\n**Tips for mixing collectibles:**\n\n1. **Choose a unifying theme**: Select collectibles that share a common theme, such as retro toys, vintage books, or items related to a specific era or genre.\n2. **Create a visual connection**: Use visual elements, like color, texture, or shape, to connect the different collectibles and create a sense of harmony.\n3. **Balance the display**: Balance the number and size of the collectibles to create a visually appealing display that's easy to navigate.\n4. **Group similar items together**: Group similar collectibles together, such as all the vintage action figures or all the books, to create a sense of organization and cohesion.\n5. **Leave some breathing room**: Leave some space between the collectibles to create a sense of breathability and avoid visual overload.\n\nIn your case, if you want to add your vintage Transformers action figure and the rare book about ancient civilizations to the shelf, consider the following:\n\n* Are the Transformers action figure and Star Wars action figures both vintage and retro-themed? If so, they might work well together.\n* Does the rare book about ancient civilizations fit with the retro-futuristic or sci-fi theme of the Star Wars action figures? If not, it might be better to display it separately.\n* Can you find a way to visually connect the different collectibles, such as using a similar color scheme or display style?\n\nUltimately, it's up to you to decide how to display your collectibles. Just remember to have fun and be mindful of the visual flow and cohesion of the display!\nUser turn 11: I think I'll try to group similar items together and create a visual connection between them. I'll start by placing the vintage Transformers action figure next to the Star Wars action figures, and see how it looks. If it works, I might add the rare book about ancient civilizations to the shelf as well, but I'll make sure it's not overwhelming the display. Thanks for the tips!\nAssistant turn 12: That's a great approach! Grouping similar items together and creating a visual connection between them can help create a cohesive and visually appealing display. By starting with the vintage Transformers action figure next to the Star Wars action figures, you can create a nostalgic and retro-themed section that celebrates your love for classic sci-fi and action figures.\n\nRemember to pay attention to the visual flow and balance of the display as you add more items. You can always adjust the arrangement to create a sense of harmony and make sure each item gets the attention it deserves.\n\nAdding the rare book about ancient civilizations can be a great way to add depth and variety to the display, but make sure it doesn't overwhelm the other items. You might consider placing it on a separate shelf or in a nearby display case to create a sense of separation and importance.\n\nMost importantly, have fun with it and enjoy the process of curating your display! It's a reflection of your personality and passions, and it's okay to experiment and try out different arrangements until you find one that feels just right.\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further guidance, feel free to ask. Otherwise, I hope you'll share a photo of your display once it's complete. I'd love to see how it turns out!\n\n=== Session 49 [Time: 2025-01-11 08:42] ===\nUser turn 1: I'm looking for some advice on interior design. I've been trying to create a cozier atmosphere in my living room, and I was thinking of adding some new decorative pieces. Do you have any suggestions? By the way, I rearranged the furniture in the living room about a month ago, swapping the positions of the armchair and the coffee table, and it's made a huge difference.\nAssistant turn 2: I'm thrilled to hear that rearranging the furniture made a big impact on your living room! That's often the simplest and most effective way to refresh a space.\n\nNow, let's talk about adding some cozy decorative pieces to enhance the ambiance. Here are some suggestions:\n\n1. **Textiles**: Throws, blankets, and pillows in soft, plush materials like wool, fleece, or Sherpa can instantly add warmth and coziness to your space. Choose materials and colors that complement your existing furniture and decor.\n2. **Rugs**: A new area rug can define the seating area and add warmth underfoot. Opt for a rug with a soft, thick pile or a natural fiber like jute or sisal.\n3. **Lighting**: Table lamps, floor lamps, or string lights can create a warm glow and make the space feel more inviting. Consider using warm-toned metal or wooden fixtures to add to the cozy vibe.\n4. **Nature-inspired elements**: Bring the outdoors in by adding natural elements like potted plants, a vase with fresh flowers, or a bowl of river rocks. This will help create a sense of calm and connection to nature.\n5. **Artwork and prints**: Hang warm, cozy-inspired artwork or prints featuring nature scenes, abstract patterns, or soft colors. This can help create a sense of comfort and relaxation.\n6. **Woven baskets**: Use woven baskets or wicker storage units to add texture and warmth to your space. They can also help hide clutter and keep the room organized.\n7. **Scented candles or essential oils**: A pleasant scent can greatly impact the ambiance of a room. Choose calming scents like vanilla, lavender, or cedarwood to create a cozy atmosphere.\n8. **Cozy accents**: Add decorative accents like vintage or antique items, such as old books, vintage cameras, or distressed wood decor, to create a sense of character and warmth.\n\nRemember, the key to creating a cozy atmosphere is to focus on comfort, texture, and warmth. Experiment with different elements and see what works best for your space and personal style.\n\nWhat do you think? Is there a particular style or aesthetic you're aiming for in your living room?\nUser turn 3: I like the idea of adding textiles and rugs to create a cozier atmosphere. Do you have any recommendations for rug sizes or materials that would work well with my current furniture arrangement?\nAssistant turn 4: Textiles and rugs can make a huge impact on the coziness of your living room.\n\nFor rug size, it's essential to consider the dimensions of your furniture and the room itself. Here are some general guidelines:\n\n1. **Room size**: A larger room can accommodate a larger rug, while a smaller room is better suited for a smaller rug. A good rule of thumb is to leave about 12-18 inches of floor space between the rug and the walls.\n2. **Furniture arrangement**: Measure the length and width of your furniture pieces, including the armchair and coffee table. A good starting point is to choose a rug that fits under the front legs of the furniture, with some extra space around the edges. This creates a sense of cohesion and defines the seating area.\n\nFor your current furniture arrangement, you might consider the following rug sizes:\n\n* A smaller rug (around 5x7 feet) that fits under the armchair and coffee table, creating a cozy nook.\n* A medium-sized rug (around 8x10 feet) that spans the entire seating area, including the armchair, coffee table, and possibly a sofa (if you have one).\n\nAs for rug materials, here are some popular options that can add warmth and coziness to your space:\n\n1. **Wool**: A classic choice, wool rugs are soft, durable, and resistant to stains. They come in a variety of natural colors and can add a warm, organic feel to your room.\n2. **Jute**: Jute rugs are made from natural fibers and have a warm, earthy look. They're also relatively affordable and can add a cozy, organic feel to your space.\n3. **Shag**: Shag rugs are known for their plush, soft piles, which can create a cozy atmosphere. Look for rugs with a shorter pile (around 1-2 inches) for a more subtle look.\n4. **Moroccan-inspired**: Moroccan-style rugs often feature a mix of natural materials, like wool and jute, and have a warm, earthy color palette. They can add a cozy, global-inspired feel to your room.\n\nSome popular rug patterns that can add coziness to your space include:\n\n1. **Natural fibers**: Rugs with a natural fiber look, like jute or sisal, can add warmth and texture to your space.\n2. **Plaid or tweed**: Plaid or tweed patterns can create a cozy, rustic feel, especially in earthy colors like beige, brown, or green.\n3. **Berber-inspired**: Berber-style rugs often feature a subtle, geometric pattern and a natural color palette, which can add a cozy, organic feel to your room.\n\nRemember, the key is to choose a rug that complements your furniture and personal style. You can also consider layering a smaller rug over a larger one to add texture and visual interest.\n\nDo any of these options resonate with you, or would you like more specific recommendations based on your personal style and furniture arrangement?\nUser turn 5: I'm thinking of getting a rug that's around 8x10 feet to fit the entire seating area. I'm drawn to Moroccan-inspired rugs, but I'm not sure if they'll clash with the new floor lamp I installed a few weeks ago. The lamp has a pretty modern design, so I want to make sure the rug will complement it.\nAssistant turn 6: An 8x10 foot rug will definitely help to define the seating area and create a cozy atmosphere.\n\nMoroccan-inspired rugs can be a great choice, but it's understandable that you're concerned about clashing with your modern floor lamp. Here are a few tips to help you choose a Moroccan-inspired rug that will complement your lamp:\n\n1. **Neutralize the pattern**: Opt for a Moroccan-inspired rug with a more subtle, neutral pattern. Look for rugs with a simpler, more geometric design, rather than intricate, busy patterns. This will help the rug blend with your modern lamp.\n2. **Choose a muted color palette**: Select a rug with a muted, earthy color palette that won't compete with the modern design of your lamp. Consider colors like beige, cream, gray, or taupe, which will provide a neutral background for your lamp.\n3. **Consider a transitional design**: Transitional rugs blend traditional and modern elements, making them a great choice if you want to combine a Moroccan-inspired design with a modern lamp. Look for rugs with a mix of geometric patterns and subtle, organic shapes.\n4. **Add a border**: A rug with a border can help to tie in the modern design of your lamp. Opt for a rug with a simple, thin border in a contrasting color to create a cohesive look.\n\nSome popular Moroccan-inspired rug styles that might work well with your modern lamp include:\n\n1. **Beni Ourain**: Beni Ourain rugs are known for their simple, geometric patterns and neutral color palette. They're a great choice if you want a Moroccan-inspired rug that won't overwhelm your modern lamp.\n2. **Azilal**: Azilal rugs feature a mix of geometric patterns and organic shapes, making them a great choice for a transitional design. They often have a more subtle, muted color palette that will complement your lamp.\n3. **Boucherouite**: Boucherouite rugs are known for their colorful, playful designs, but you can also find more muted, neutral options that will work well with your lamp.\n\nRemember, the key is to find a rug that complements your lamp without overpowering it. You can also consider ordering a rug sample or seeing the rug in person before making a final decision.\n\nDo any of these options resonate with you, or would you like more specific recommendations based on your lamp's design and color scheme?\nUser turn 7: I think a Moroccan-inspired rug with a neutral color palette and a simpler pattern would work well with my modern floor lamp. I also like the idea of a transitional design that blends traditional and modern elements. Can you give me some suggestions on where to find these types of rugs, and what kind of budget I should expect?\nAssistant turn 8: A Moroccan-inspired rug with a neutral color palette and a simpler pattern will provide a beautiful backdrop for your modern floor lamp. Transitional designs are also a great way to blend traditional and modern elements. Here are some suggestions on where to find these types of rugs and what kind of budget you can expect:\n\n**Online Retailers:**\n\n1. **West Elm**: West Elm offers a wide selection of Moroccan-inspired rugs with neutral color palettes and simpler patterns. They often have a range of transitional designs that blend traditional and modern elements. Budget: $200-$1,000.\n2. **Crate & Barrel**: Crate & Barrel features a variety of Moroccan-inspired rugs with modern twists. They often have a range of neutral color palettes and simpler patterns. Budget: $200-$1,500.\n3. **Wayfair**: Wayfair is an online retailer that carries a vast selection of rugs from various brands. You can filter by style, color, and price to find the perfect Moroccan-inspired rug for your space. Budget: $100-$2,000.\n4. **Rugs USA**: Rugs USA is an online retailer that specializes in rugs. They offer a wide selection of Moroccan-inspired rugs with neutral color palettes and simpler patterns. Budget: $100-$1,500.\n\n**Specialty Rug Stores:**\n\n1. **Local Moroccan or Middle Eastern import stores**: If you have a local store that specializes in Moroccan or Middle Eastern imports, they may carry a selection of authentic, handmade Moroccan rugs. These rugs can be more expensive, but they're often one-of-a-kind pieces. Budget: $500-$5,000.\n2. **High-end home decor stores**: Luxury home decor stores like Design Within Reach or Mitchell Gold + Bob Williams may carry high-end, Moroccan-inspired rugs with modern twists. Budget: $1,000-$10,000.\n\n**Budget:**\n\nFor a high-quality, Moroccan-inspired rug with a neutral color palette and a simpler pattern, you can expect to pay between $200-$2,000. If you're looking for a more luxurious, handmade rug, prices can range from $500-$10,000.\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Read reviews**: Before making a purchase, read reviews from other customers to get a sense of the rug's quality and durability.\n2. **Check the materials**: Make sure the rug is made from high-quality materials that will withstand foot traffic and cleaning.\n3. **Consider the pile height**: A lower pile height (around 1/4 inch) is often preferred for high-traffic areas, while a higher pile height (around 1/2 inch) can add more comfort and texture to a room.\n4. **Look for sales and discounts**: Keep an eye out for sales and discounts, especially during holiday weekends or special promotions.\n\nI hope this helps you in your search for the perfect Moroccan-inspired rug!\nUser turn 9: I'm going to check out West Elm and Crate & Barrel online to see what kind of Moroccan-inspired rugs they have. I'll also look into local Moroccan import stores in my area to see if they have any authentic, handmade rugs. Thanks for the suggestions and budget guidance!\nAssistant turn 10: You're welcome! I'm glad I could help. West Elm and Crate & Barrel are both great resources for Moroccan-inspired rugs, and you may find some beautiful options that fit your style and budget.\n\nAdditionally, exploring local Moroccan import stores can be a great way to find unique, handmade rugs that will add a touch of authenticity to your space. Just keep in mind that prices may vary depending on the quality, materials, and craftsmanship of the rug.\n\nRemember to take your time, do your research, and don't hesitate to reach out to customer service or ask questions if you need more information. It's also a good idea to read reviews, check the return policies, and consider the warranty or guarantee offered by the retailer.\n\nMost importantly, have fun with the process! Finding the right rug can be a great way to enhance the coziness and style of your living room.\n\nIf you have any more questions or need further guidance, feel free to ask. Good luck with your rug hunt, and I hope you find the perfect one for your space!\nUser turn 11: Wait, I think I got a bit carried away there. As a user, I would simply say:\n\n\"Thanks for the suggestions and budget guidance! I'll definitely check out West Elm and Crate & Barrel online, and look into local Moroccan import stores in my area. I'll let you know if I have any more questions or need further assistance.\"\nAssistant turn 12: You're absolutely right! I apologize for the mistake. Your response is a perfect example of how a user would respond in a conversation. It's concise, clear, and shows appreciation for the guidance provided.\n\nHere's the revised response:\n\n\"Thanks for the suggestions and budget guidance! I'll definitely check out West Elm and Crate & Barrel online, and look into local Moroccan import stores in my area. I'll let you know if I have any more questions or need further assistance.\"\n\nI'll make sure to keep this in mind for future conversations. Thank you for correcting me!\n\nQuestion: I’m picking out a couple of books at the library this week—what kind of books make the most sense for me to come home with right now?\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object:\n{\n  \"old_state\": \"...\",\n  \"new_state\": \"...\",\n  \"change_type\": \"DIRECT | PROPAGATED | UNKNOWN\",\n  \"status\": \"OBSERVED | INFERRED | UNRESOLVED\",\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\"...\"]\n}\nUse at most 3 compact evidence_refs in `Session N, User/Assistant turn M` form.\nDo not quote full messages in evidence_refs."}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "max_tokens": 256, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}, "stream": false}